# The one point this module is pinned to.
#
# Read by `sim` for both halves of what it sets up — the code under `upstream/`
# and the dataset under `.cache/data` — because the two have to come from the
# same commit. The simulator reads its data by file name and by shape, so code
# and data from different commits give a result comparable with nothing.
#
# To move to another commit: edit COMMIT here, then
#
#     ./simulator/sim restore --force     # the code, re-downloaded
#     ./simulator/sim fetch --force       # the data, re-downloaded
#
# Both say what they changed. `sim status` afterwards confirms the two agree.

